155 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 109 0 R
/E (The most frequently documented barriers were switched-off phones \(47\), not available \(42\), and no answer \(40\). Additional barriers included movement to another location \(15\), lack of network coverage \(11\), wrong numbers \(2\), and refusal \(2\). These patterns indicate that difficulties in contacting households were a significant operational constraint during household data collection.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
